          "title": "Problem 7.5: Numerical reconstruction. Starting with the parameters in Lesson ",
          "statement": "**Numerical reconstruction.** Starting with the parameters in Lesson 7.1, repeat the numerical result and then calculate one new operating point obtained by changing only one parameter by 10%. Identify a physical limit or source of uncertainty not included in the initial equation.\n\n**Diagnostic challenge.** What information is missing from the aver...",
          "solution": "**Diagnostic challenge.** What information is missing from the averaged model when selecting a voltage probe bandwidth? Write one observable signal whose change would support the diagnosis and another whose change would contradict it. State whether the correct experiment needs a cycle-average, RMS, peak or instantaneous waveform measurement.\n\n**Reference answer and marking guidance.** The original case is as follows: With Vin=24 V, d=0.5 and R=6 ohms, equilibrium voltage is 12 V and inductor current is 2 A. For L=100 microhenrys and C=470 microfarads, the undamped LC natural frequency is 1/(2\u03c0\u221aLC)\u2248734 Hz before including load damping and parasitics. A correct solution must restate the equation or conservation argument before evaluating it. The requested 10% extension depends on the chosen parameter and must state what is held constant. A response that ignores the limitation\u2014Averaging filters out switching ripple; it cannot predict MOSFET commutation spikes or subharmonic instability of a specific peak-current-mode controller without extra states.\u2014is incomplete. Award credit for identifying the correct domain, not for inventing physical readings that were never measured."
